# .gitignore
#
# PRINCIPLE: results are opt-OUT, never opt-in.
#
# The previous version ignored `*.json` wholesale. The experiment drivers worked
# around it with `git add -f`, but the analysis scripts had no such escape, and
# 15 files went missing without a single warning:
#
#     ep_exp4_*.json  (12)   episode-level bootstrap, exp4
#     ep_exp5_*.json  ( 3)   episode-level bootstrap, exp5
#
# Those are the corrected standard errors the paper quotes. `git status` never
# mentioned them because ignored files are invisible by design. Any rule broad
# enough to swallow a result silently is a defect, so this file ignores only
# things that are (a) regenerable from what IS committed, (b) machine-local, or
# (c) enormous.
#
# ANTI-RULES - patterns deliberately NOT used, and why:
#
#   *token*   matches scripts/tokenizer_check.py, which verifies the
#             single-token filler and the 34/39/45 parity targets. A pattern
#             with no slash matches the BASENAME AT ANY DEPTH. This would have
#             deleted the evidence for the study's central methodological claim.
#   *secret*  same class of error. Credentials are kept out of the working tree
#             entirely (export in the shell), which no pattern can guarantee.
#   *.json    see above.
#   calib.json / sweep.json
#             provenance for the calibrated block widths. Committed.
#   *.sqlite.gz
#             ~868 MB and already in history. Ignoring them now would do nothing
#             (ignore rules do not affect tracked files) and removing them would
#             require rewriting history, which would invalidate every
#             run_meta.git_commit recorded across exp1-exp5.

# ---- environments and caches (regenerable) --------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# ---- SQLite ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The uncompressed DB is never committed; the .gz beside it is. WAL and SHM are
# transient and committing one produces a corrupt-looking database on checkout.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-journal

# ---- run-local markers ----------------------------------------------------
# The exp6 driver touches ${tag}.done for resume-after-crash. Pod-local state.
*.done

# ---- model weights --------------------------------------------------------
# Gigabytes each, fetched from HF by model_id. Committing one exceeds GitHub's
# 100 MB per-file hard limit and the push is rejected outright.
*.safetensors
*.gguf
*.pt
*.pth
models/
hf_cache/

# ---- credentials ----------------------------------------------------------
# Backstop only. Tokens must be exported in the shell and never written to disk
# inside the repo. A pattern is not a security control.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
id_rsa*

# ---- editor / OS ----------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~